The first complete implementation at `2cd2d44b9d190db08931ae7bf516a768230d81ba` compiled and its new admission regression printed PASS, but run `37047348927`, job `110972315883`, timed out in the full Core suite. Root cause: a simple global System Optimization mutex made the existing `GenericGuardianSystemOptimizationActivityIntegrationSelfTests.DuringMutation` nested second transaction wait on the first transaction that was synchronously waiting for the nested operation. This was treated as a real regression, not GREEN.

